-  "effective_date": "September 30, 2026",
-  "body_html": "<p><em>Effective date: September 30, 2026</em></p>\n<p>These Terms and Conditions (these \"Terms\") govern your use of the website at valorahq.com, including all content, tools, calculators, and services offered through it (collectively, the \"Site\"). The Site is operated by SpacesOS Inc. (\"Valora,\" \"we,\" \"us,\" or \"our\"). By accessing or using the Site, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Site.</p>\n<h2>United States users only</h2>\n<p>The Site is directed at, and intended for, individuals located in the United States. The content and services described on the Site are oriented to the United States market, United States law, and United States financial regulation. If you access the Site from outside the United States, you do so on your own initiative and are responsible for compliance with the laws of your jurisdiction.</p>\n<h2>What Valora is, and what it is not</h2>\n<p>Valora publishes educational information about financial planning and provides an inquiry route through which you can tell us what you are trying to figure out. We review each request by hand and respond by email. Valora is not a registered investment adviser, broker-dealer, law firm, or accounting firm, and the Site does not provide investment, legal, tax, accounting, or financial advice.</p>\n<p>Valora does not currently operate a public advisor directory, and we are not arranging advisor matches or introductions. Any advisor or firm mentioned in our educational content is independent, is not an employee, agent, partner, or representative of Valora, and is not endorsed by us.</p>\n<h2>No professional advice and no professional relationship</h2>\n<p>All content on the Site, including articles, guides, and calculator results, is provided for general informational and educational purposes only. It does not take into account your objectives, financial situation, or needs, and it is not a recommendation, offer, or solicitation to buy or sell any security or to adopt any strategy.</p>\n<p>Your use of the Site, including submitting a request form, does not create an advisory, fiduciary, attorney-client, accountant-client, or any other professional relationship between you and Valora. No attorney-client relationship is created by anything on this Site or by contacting us. If you engage an advisor now or in the future, that relationship is solely between you and the advisor, under the terms you agree with them.</p>\n<p>Before making any financial, legal, or tax decision, consult a qualified professional who understands your specific circumstances.</p>\n<h2>Request forms</h2>\n<p>When you submit a request form on the Site, the information you provide is used to review your request and respond to you by email. Submissions are processed through a Google Apps Script into an internal Google Sheet, as described in our <a href=\"/privacy/\">Privacy Policy</a>. Submitting a form does not guarantee a response within any particular time, and it does not authorize us to share your answers with any advisor. We do not forward request information to advisors.</p>\n<p>If a referral or introduction service is ever offered in the future, it will be described in an updated version of these Terms before it operates.</p>\n<h2>Calculators and estimates</h2>\n<p>The calculators on the Site produce simplified estimates based on the inputs you provide and stated assumptions. They are illustrations only: they ignore many real-world variables, they are not predictions, and they must not be relied on as financial, tax, or investment advice. Actual results will differ.</p>\n<h2>Your submissions</h2>\n<p>You are responsible for the accuracy of information you submit through the Site. Please do not send us sensitive personal information such as Social Security numbers, account numbers, passwords, or full statements; the Site is not designed to receive them, and you send any such information at your own risk.</p>\n<p>By submitting c