+<section class="section section--paper" id="faq">
+  <div class="container" style="max-width:700px;">
+<div class="faq">
+      <h2 class="faq__title">Common questions</h2>
+      <details class="faq__item"><summary>Do I need a financial advisor before selling my business?</summary><p>A defined planning assignment may help connect proposed proceeds and obligations to household goals. It does not replace a transaction attorney or tax professional. Ask what would be delivered before the next decision, which facts need review and whether you can buy planning without committing future assets.</p></details>
+      <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why is the headline price different from available cash?</summary><p>The price may include amounts not received at closing, retained equity or conditional payments. Debt, fees, adjustments, taxes and remaining commitments may also affect the picture. Reconcile definitions and documents first so you do not count the same deduction twice.</p></details>
+      <details class="faq__item"><summary>Is all gain from a business sale taxed as capital gain?</summary><p>No. IRS sale-of-business guidance explains that asset sales can involve different treatment for different assets, including ordinary income or loss for inventory. Ask a tax professional to review the actual transaction, seller and asset classifications rather than apply one rate to the headline price.</p></details>
+      <details class="faq__item"><summary>Can I assume taxes on deferred proceeds wait until payment?</summary><p>No. IRS Publication 537 describes installment-sale conditions and exceptions, including inventory and depreciation recapture. Escrow and contingent payments also need fact-specific review. Ask a tax professional to compare payment timing with recognition and payment obligations.</p></details>
+      <details class="faq__item"><summary>What should I ask about the advisor&#x27;s fees before the sale?</summary><p>Ask for the planning fee, exclusions, costs if the transaction changes or fails, and any later management fees. Ask whether compensation changes when proceeds move into management and whether there are referral or affiliated-product incentives. Compare the agreement and applicable disclosures.</p></details>
+      <details class="faq__item"><summary>Does this page value my business or arrange an introduction?</summary><p>No. The worksheet organizes questions; it does not calculate valuation, tax or a suitable portfolio. Valora is not arranging advisor matches or introductions at this time. Verify any professional&#x27;s scope, experience and disclosures independently.</p></details>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+</section>
